{"numberOfHits":1,"results":[{"id":"GO:0098669","isObsolete":false,"name":"superinfection exclusion","definition":{"text":"The process by which a preexisting viral infection prevents a secondary infection with the same or a closely related virus. Typically some aspect of viral entry is inhibited, but post entry mechanisms have also been documented.","xrefs":[{"dbCode":"PMID","dbId":"11985726"},{"dbCode":"PMID","dbId":"23692331"},{"dbCode":"PMID","dbId":"24089557"},{"dbCode":"PMID","dbId":"8012757"},{"dbCode":"VZ","dbId":"3971"}]},"history":[{"timestamp":"2024-09-05","action":"Added","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2022-11-22","action":"Added","category":"DEFINITION","text":"The process by which a preexisting viral infection prevents a secondary infection with the same or a closely related virus. Typically some aspect of viral entry is inhibited, but post entry mechanisms have also been documented."},{"timestamp":"2022-11-22","action":"Deleted","category":"DEFINITION","text":"The process by which a preexisting viral infection prevents a secondary infection with the same or a closely related virus.  Typically some aspect of viral entry is inhibited, but post entry mechanisms have also been documented."},{"timestamp":"2017-01-21","action":"Added","category":"DEFINITION","text":"The process by which a preexisting viral infection prevents a secondary infection with the same or a closely related virus.  Typically some aspect of viral entry is inhibited, but post entry mechanisms have also been documented."},{"timestamp":"2017-01-21","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0016032 (viral process)"},{"timestamp":"2017-01-21","action":"Added","category":"XREF","text":"VZ:3971"},{"timestamp":"2017-01-21","action":"Added","category":"TERM","text":"superinfection exclusion"}],"xRefs":[{"dbCode":"UniProtKB-KW","dbId":"KW-1260","name":"Superinfection exclusion"},{"dbCode":"VZ","dbId":"3971"}],"taxonConstraints":[{"ancestorId":"GO:0098669","ancestorName":"superinfection exclusion","relationship":"never_in_taxon","taxId":"4896","taxIdType":"NCBITaxon","taxName":"Schizosaccharomyces pombe"}],"aspect":"biological_process","usage":"Unrestricted","goDiscussions":[{"title":"Viral Processes","url":"http://wiki.geneontology.org/index.php/Virus_terms"}]}],"pageInfo":null}